A fact is one self-contained sentence that states one claim. Write each fact so a reader understands it alone: name
the people, companies, and documents it is about instead of "this Agreement", "the Company", "he", or "they". Keep
who said it, and keep conditions, hedges, and negations. Skip headings, boilerplate, and filler.

